2026-10-11T04:34:26.2056659Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2065485Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2153828Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2162753Z [0m
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2163266Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2163833Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2164360Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2164658Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2165236Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2165601Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2165927Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2166578Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2166793Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2167322Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2167967Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2168528Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2168892Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2169022Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2169211Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2169417Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2169648Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2169968Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2170072Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2170172Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2170490Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2170788Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2171187Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2173063Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2173182Z I will:
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2173287Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2173456Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2173805Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2174163Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2174487Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2174707Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2174938Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2175504Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2175978Z    /root
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2333945Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2334590Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2347752Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2348398Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2348732Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2349087Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2349557Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2362011Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2362989Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2372028Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2372698Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2373077Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2373240Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2373399Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2373583Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2373795Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2374143Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2374312Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2374406Z If you would like to
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2374653Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2374819Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2375043Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2375416Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2375549Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2375565Z 
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2375773Z [32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
2026-10-11T04:34:26.2383001Z [0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
